---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Lampleaf Terms of Use"
      description="Terms of Use for Lampleaf, an illustrated Bible app for iPhone and iPad."
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main id="main">
      <article class="policy tile">
        <p class="tile-kicker">Lampleaf</p>
        <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="date"><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 19, 2026</p>

        <p>
          Lampleaf is an illustrated Bible app for iPhone and iPad: Scripture on one page, and a
          picture, study notes, your own notes or narration beside it. By using the app, you agree
          to use it lawfully and in accordance with these terms and Apple's
          <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >Licensed Application End User License Agreement</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Free to read</h2>
        <p>
          The complete Bible in every included translation is free to read, search, highlight and
          take notes on, with no account. Reading plans are optional schedules; they never lock or
          limit what you can read.
        </p>

        <h2>Lampleaf Plus</h2>
        <p>
          When it is offered, Lampleaf Plus is a single one-time in-app purchase, not a
          subscription. It adds extras such as additional bindings and media; it never restricts
          reading Scripture. Purchases are made through Apple, and Apple's terms govern payment,
          billing and refunds. Refunds are requested from Apple; this app cannot issue them. Nothing
          in these terms limits refund or consumer rights you have under the law where you live.
        </p>

        <h2>The Bible text and what accompanies it</h2>
        <p>
          The included translations (the Berean Standard Bible, the King James Version and the World
          English Bible) are public domain. Narration is generated from the exact text of each
          translation and reviewed before release. Pictures are public-domain artworks credited by
          artist and year. Original-language word data comes from STEP Bible under CC BY 4.0. Full
          credits are in the app under Settings, Acknowledgements.
        </p>
        <p>
          Study notes, summaries and answers to common questions are helps written to explain the
          text. They are not Scripture and not a final authority. Where Christians read a passage in
          more than one way, Lampleaf aims to describe the main views fairly; please read with your
          own church and conscience.
        </p>

        <h2>Your notes</h2>
        <p>
          Notes and highlights you make are yours. This app claims no ownership of them and does not
          upload them. They are stored on your device, so they can be lost if the app is deleted,
          the device is lost, or its storage fails. The app does not operate a cloud backup.
        </p>

        <h2>Lampleaf itself</h2>
        <p>
          The app, its design, the original study notes and the narration recordings remain the
          property of the developer. You may use them within the app and share verses and notes
          through the app's sharing features. Please do not republish the app's original content as
          your own product.
        </p>

        <h2>What the app is not</h2>
        <p>
          Lampleaf is a Bible reading and study app. It is not counseling, therapy, medical advice
          or pastoral care, and it is not a substitute for professional help or your church.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
        <p>
          Features and content may change as the app develops; narration and pictures are added a
          chapter at a time. The app is provided as it is, without a promise that it will be
          uninterrupted or error free.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:randyventures06@gmail.com">randyventures06@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .date {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
